\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. What shall I do my God to love,
\par My Saviour, and the world's to praise?
\par Whose tenderest compassions move
\par To me and all the fallen race,
\par Whose mercy is divinely free
\par For all the fallen race and- me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I long to know, and to make known,
\par The heights and depths of love divine,
\par The kindness Thou to me hast shown,
\par Whose every sin was counted Thine:
\par My God for me resigned His breath;
\par He died to save my soul from death.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. How shall I thank Thee for the grace
\par On me and all mankind bestowed?
\par O that my every breath were praise!
\par O that my heart were filled with God!
\par My heart would then with love o'erflow,
\par And all my life Thy glory show.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

